      "message": "@lehoangquyen@chromium.org\nThe idea of this attempting CL to get the alignment value from the device at runtime seemingly would not be an elegant way. The corresponding value currently in Dawn is the constant [kTextureBytesPerRowAlignment](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/dawn/src/dawn/common/Constants.h;drc\u003d981ce1e8f82050b33153a9c4652f2ad1cefabff1;l\u003d44), which is already used widely in many places. It would be troublesome to replace them all by querying from the device. Any suggestions?",
      "revId": "ab9ee1ecb9c00cfc6baae780e07be9f3dd430b9f",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
